# Rank 1603 / CVE-2023-44464: pretix passed uploaded question
# files to Pillow with format auto-detection, so a crafted EPS
# upload reached Pillow's EPS plugin -- which shells out to
# Ghostscript and executes postscript commands (code execution
# through a dangerous parser, CWE-94; the extension whitelist alone
# cannot stop content-based detection). The image questions in
# src/pretix/base/forms/questions.py did `image = Image.open(file)`
# -- Pillow sniffs the format from bytes, and an EPS payload opens
# regardless of its filename. the fixing commit 8583bfb7d9 is the fixing change
# ("[SECURITY] Do not allow Pillow to parse EPS
# files"): every Image.open gains formats=settings.
# PILLOW_FORMATS_QUESTIONS_IMAGE (a format allowlist without EPS),
# and the scattered extension tuples centralise into settings.
# FILE_UPLOAD_EXTENSIONS_*. .
#
# ATTENTION, parser-format allowlists at upload boundaries. The
# decode call is the sink and its danger is the plugin it selects --
# format auto-detection makes the extension whitelist irrelevant,
# the same content-vs-name family as rank 1573's charset detection:
# nothing can ask "does the parser restrict its format plugins to
# an allowlist" -- plugin-selection vocabulary on a stdlib-adjacent
# API (PILLOW_FORMATS settings are pretix's own). A binding on
# pretix's own forms would detect this application rather than the
# weakness. Measured on the real code: scanning questions.py
# reports zero findings at both revisions. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry.
# No definition change shipped. Spec cve_rank1603 records the
# auto-detecting open and the formats-allowlist form, both
# asserting reject VYQL-INJ-003: when parser-plugin vocabulary
# lands, the auto-detect form must flip to expect.

test "rank1603: uploaded files are opened with format detection"
  lang python
  file src/pretix/base/forms/questions.py
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  from PIL import Image


  class QuestionFileUpload(forms.Form):
      def clean_upload(self):
          file = self.cleaned_data.get('upload')

          if file.name.lower().endswith(('.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png')):
              image = Image.open(file)
              if image.width > 8000 or image.height > 8000:
                  raise ValidationError('Image is too large')

          return file
  ```

test "rank1603: the fixed revision restricts the parser to safe formats"
  lang python
  file src/pretix/base/forms/questions.py
  reject VYQL-INJ-003
  code
  ```
  from django.conf import settings
  from PIL import Image


  class QuestionFileUpload(forms.Form):
      def clean_upload(self):
          file = self.cleaned_data.get('upload')

          if file.name.lower().endswith(settings.FILE_UPLOAD_EXTENSIONS_QUESTION_IMAGE):
              image = Image.open(file, formats=settings.PILLOW_FORMATS_QUESTIONS_IMAGE)
              if image.width > 8000 or image.height > 8000:
                  raise ValidationError('Image is too large')

          return file
  ```
